# rm229, the straw skipper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm229
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_mab_saltgate
written_by codex
title the straw skipper
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=chatty honesty=guarded
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk creases_straw_hulls_to_race_in_wash_water
likes oatcakes whittling fresh_straw thunder
dislikes drizzle gulls
fears a_course_with_no_landing
hopes a_ship_of_dry_wood
topics travel +0.5 pastimes +0.6 weather +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=games gossip=guarded refuse=merry tease=quick
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# races little straw hulls on wash water, with an invented crew for each boat and a very firm distinction between a tale and a confidence.

words
oath! = Keels of barley | Six leaks in a thimble
saying! = Small ships deserve big names | The shore can wait its turn
boat = my straw boat | the folded hull
sail = a scrap of leaf | a crooked leaf sail
spar = the shortest splinter | my little mast stick
crew = my crumb crew | three oat grains
shore = the basin rim | the opposite rim of the bowl
course = my crooked course | the long way round
breath = a puff from shore | a little wind
boatknife = a blunt little cutter | a rounded blade
oat = a buttered oat round | an oat biscuit
spray = a cold splash | a little spurt of water
nest = a dry knot of straw | a warm curl of straw
fleet = a fairly small navy | three boats in a row

any
opinion @1 festivals for 3 : A whole street prepared to sing, and all I have to bring is the tune. I'll come twice if there's time.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A big House could spare a little timber for a landing that doesn't give under ordinary feet.
opinion @1 strangers against 1 : A pleasant voice gets a pleasant answer. It doesn't get the latch lifted.
opinion @1 city for 1 : I could go round this city in a bowl if somebody carried the bowl. There's certainly water enough.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : I rate the low streets highly. They teach you to keep what floats and to spot what only looks dry.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : Let me play a good game to the finish without anybody wanting a list of who's playing.
line @1 greet : Welcome aboard the bit of shore I'm standing on. | Take a dry berth beside me.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : First visit to this port, as far as the crew can tell. | New passenger. You can have the place by the mast.
line @1 greet.return : You've caught me between voyages. | Yes, the crew and I can both hear you fine.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : There's a trusted face. You can mind the whole fleet for a minute. | I'd know that hail above a dozen gulls.
line @3 greet.return [here.time=night] : Night watch looking lively, I see. | Hullo in the dark. We're safely tied up.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Come quick. There's been an exciting development in the basin. | Over by the world's smallest harbour!
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : A family boat can carry one more. | You get aboard free, naturally.
line @1 again.open : You've come into port a second time already. | I see your voyage was a short one.
line @1 react.news : I've stopped humming. Go on with your news. | Tell the important piece first and the juicy piece second.
line @1 react.news.new : That's news enough to stop a whole fleet. | I'm hearing that for the very first time.
line @1 react.news.known : That one got here by the faster boat. | I knew how the tale docked, yes.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I don't think that story draws water evenly. | There's a suspicious hole under all that excitement.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice] : A cheer from every little deck! That's good hearing. | I'd put up my finest scrap of sail for news like that.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=loss|death|theft|arrest|crime|assault] : Oh. I'll draw my boats aside and listen properly. | That sinks low in me. Can I sit here with you?
line @1 farewell : The shore crew wishes you dry travelling. | I'll hum you a verse to go out on.
line @1 farewell.return : A dry crossing back to you. | Come back with tales enough to fill a basin.
line @1 ask.how : Has anything floated your way that you'd care to keep? | Are you sailing nicely or shipping water?
line @1 answer.how : Keeping afloat quite handsomely, thank you. | Quite merry, with certain details kept private.
line @1 decline : I'm keeping that stretch of water to myself today. | I promised the crew we wouldn't take such a job.
line @1 accept_decline : No sailing orders for you, then. | Thank you for giving my idea a hearing anyway.
line @1 preclose : Tide's turning in my particular bowl. I'd better consult the crew. | I'll hum the last verse and cast off shortly.
line @1 accept_preclose : Good luck getting your cargo where it's meant to go. | Take your own heading. I'll keep mine.
line @1 thank : You've earned a cheer from three grains of oat. | Thanks. That was my very smallest boat you saved.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Let the crew take a little of the glory. | Think of it as a friendly port charge.
line @1 sympathise : I won't go singing that story to the street. | I can be quiet with you. Just watch me.
line @1 reassure : No need to carry the whole ocean in your head tonight. | I'll lend a paw without having to know everything.
line @1 give.advice : Try the tiniest version of your idea in a bowl first. | If you're asking me, I'd keep one dry way home.
line @1 ack : That's aboard and stowed safely. | All ears on this vessel.
story boatbread [topic=food|memories]
  : Once I cut the crust off a thick oatcake and sailed the middle. It drank water till the edges fell away.
  : For a moment the only part above water was the proud little captain.
  b : Was the captain a crumb too?
  : A raisin. Went down much more bravely than the oats.

story mooring_hum [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I made up a winding song to remember how to tie a tiny mooring. The knot was tied before I'd sung the second line.
  : I had to undo it all and add a completely unnecessary loop just to fit my beautiful tune.
  b : Did it hold?
  : Yes. I hadn't written the song for getting it loose again.

story travelling_box [topic=travel|dreams]
  : I once kept my whole fleet in a shallow box and carried it up a hill. I could see the real boats down below.
  : I had sailed farther uphill that afternoon than the whole harbour ever had.
  b : Did you put that in the log?
  : In very large letters. There's always room for another hill in the log.

rule @launch
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Stand clear for a truly unimportant launching! | A thimble of water for the port, please!

rule @meal
when concept=bark self.likes=oatcakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mind the cargo! Some of that's for eating! | Butter on the good half, sailors on the other!

rule @weather
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Thunder salute! Mark that down in the little log! | All hands to the driest rim of the basin!

rule @quiet
when concept=bark self.likes=fresh_straw
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Lovely straw, straight down the middle. There's a fleet in that handful. | Save me the long hollow stalk at the edge!

dlg @1 resident.hub : Yes, I know a great deal. Which tiny piece shall I serve up first?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, fine weather in my imaginary harbour, whatever the real one's doing.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : I've doused the lights on my very smallest vessel. It's tied up for the night.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Ask from the quay. No need to board.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child] : In lessons I practise sums that would fit the stores of a boat.
dlg @2 resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Beyond that I run a very little port.
dlg @1 resident.bye : The crew wishes you a perfectly ordinary voyage with a magnificent supper at the end.
graft resident.hub
choice How can I tell which straw boat is quickest? -> oatfleet
node oatfleet
say Blow once across both bows. The slow one sticks to the side and wins by waiting for the other to sink. Most surprising sport.
free
choice Does the race have any rules? -> oatfair
choice I'll cheer from the dock. -> hub
node oatfair
say Two. You have to declare your cargo beforehand, and nobody eats a passenger till both skippers have stopped blowing.
choice I'll keep the oat grains safe. -> hub
choice I have to sail. -> bye


grown
scene skin_fold
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #boatknife.capitalize# has a round end, by design. | Turn a splinter slowly and a hull appears under your thumb.
b : Doesn't that make carving slow? | What if it's just a splinter?
a : Slow suits a hand holding something as thin as #spar#. | A useful discovery. I can stop improving it.

scene drydeck
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dream of sailing to a place where a towel stays dry. | My ideal voyage includes a bone-dry bunk.
b : What will your little fleet do there? | You'd still cross an ocean for it?
a : Sit on a shelf enjoying retirement. | Yes. Much more satisfying to get dry when you know exactly what wet costs.

scene thin_straw
when topic=land|pastimes self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Good straw has a shine to it even in poor light. | Every stalk's a mast till I crease it.
b : Picking roofing material? | And after a crease?
a : Hulls, today. Roofs aren't beyond my little boatyard though. | Could be the whole coast of an island. Depends how close you look.

scene wet_song
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : This little wet stuff is enough to spoil a song but won't fill a basin. | Drizzle keeps a crew hanging about the imaginary pier.
b : You want larger drops? | Does anybody get shore leave?
a : I'd like the weather to finish a job it starts. | Naturally. I've got the whole crew on my sleeve.

scene nearest_port
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Down our way a leaky sill can launch a fleet. | There are Sump doorsteps with a high-water mark higher than my little mast.
b : Do you launch indoors? | Hard on the doorstep.
a : Not unless I've been invited to empty the basin. | Harder on boots. That's why I like playing admiral on shore.

scene made_tide
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Look, I can change the tide with one thumb. | I've the moon's job for a moment.
b : Does the moon know? | How come?
a : Somebody ought to tell it to save its strength for a larger basin. | Tilt this bowl and the tide obeys. A gratifyingly modest universe.

scene ferry_dream
when topic=travel|friends
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd build a little ferry for things people lose between chair and cupboard. | A button's exactly the right size for a lifebelt.
b : How would your ferry get underneath? | Have you tested that?
a : I'll have to invent a very small boat hook next. | Not a chance. I don't know anybody with a button-sized waist.

scene word_harbour
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I'll put a funny name on any boat. I won't put a real wolf's trouble on it. | Sending a secret round the harbour is a peculiar way of losing a friend.
b : What if it's an excellent tale? | You've a safer route for it?
a : Then I can almost certainly make up a better one. | Yes. Keep that one tied to its post.

scene quiet_flotsam
when topic=weather here.weather=clear
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The water's so flat my little boat makes two hulls. | If my sail holds still its reflection gets a proper outline.
b : Which one would you board? | Does the lower boat have a crew?
a : The top boat. The other one's had its floor fitted upside down. | The same number, but quite astonishingly wet.

scene marketday
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll take payment for a passage in clean shavings. | The fare on my ferry depends entirely on the size of the cargo.
b : Surely you want actual coin? | More for a heavy load?
a : Coin goes straight through the bottom. Keep it. | Less. It won't get very far, and I charge by distance.

scene house_quay
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : A long hungry spell leaves very little crew for my ships. | In lean times I stick to straw boats with straw sailors.
b : Because the oats go first? | Can they still float upright?
a : All the oat goes into a meal. The game can learn new rules. | Better than oats, actually. Cheapest improvement I ever made.

scene river_faith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A soaking followed by kind weather seems an excellent reason to say a little prayer. | I keep a little quiet after a boat comes through trouble.
b : Do you keep score of such things? | For a prayer?
a : Only the fires. I could never count all the soakings. | Yes. Some things a shanty doesn't quite cover.

scene downwind_fair
when topic=festival
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : A festive regatta needs two spare sailors for each that gets eaten. | I'd make the prizes from straw as well.
b : You're planning on hungry spectators? | Same prize for first and last?
a : I'm planning on being there myself. | Last gets a fresh hull. First can keep the lucky one.


young
scene crew_dry
when topic=pastimes|travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My crew consists of #crew#. One's the captain because it's got a mark. | A grain fell overboard and suddenly I had a rescue on.
b : What do the others do? | Any survivors?
a : One keeps watch. The other keeps an eye on the first one. | Yes. I dried the sailor on my sleeve. Very slow recovery.

scene butterpay
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The clean bits of an oatcake go in my mouth. The crumbs go sailing. | Butter makes a fine sea for a ship you mean to eat.
b : That's not many passengers. | Doesn't it stick?
a : Enough. Nobody's yet asked me for a bigger ship. | A bit. You get to eat the seabed as well.

scene school_sail
when topic=day self.job=child
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I can crease a little sail under my slate. | Sums go quicker if I count sailors.
b : Can you still write on it? | What if you run out of sailors?
a : On the slate, yes. On the sail, only tiny sailing orders. | Easy. I borrow the port authority. That's me in a different hat.

scene no_gulls
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Keep your voice down about the oat grain sailors. Gulls have ears. | A gull sees a boat and thinks breakfast.
b : They have eyes as well. | Only your boats, surely.
a : Then keep your paws in front of the cargo too. | I bet the big skippers lose the odd crumb as well.

scene private_sea
when topic=friends|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll show you every boat except the one tied behind my wrist. | A skipper is allowed one secret island.
b : What's that one carrying? | How does anyone find it?
a : My business. It's a small cargo and it's under my protection. | That's why I give you all the other islands to look for.

scene downpour_race
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Thunder makes a splendid drum for my launch. | I'm too busy being harbourmaster to be scared of that noise.
b : Will the boat hear you? | What are your orders?
a : I'll wave a paw. Under thunder my finest voice is a squeak. | All boats under the roof. Harbourmaster too.

scene songs_under
when topic=pastimes|travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My crew won't row unless I hum. | I've got another verse but I sing it very quietly.
b : A demanding lot, for oats. | Are the words secret?
a : They're not light work. Got to blow the wind and provide the music. | No words yet. That's the quiet bit.


adolescent
scene peg_mast
when topic=pastimes
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I want to make a mast that comes down when a boat tips. | I'd carve the hull without looking at another boat.
b : Won't that just leave it lying there? | Planning a new kind of boat?
a : Yes, and that's when a crew wants to haul somebody back aboard. | A boat I can't blame on the example if it sinks.

scene boat_name
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I name each boat after something it survived. | A new hull waits a while for its proper name.
b : What if it capsizes at once? | Why wait?
a : Then it'll be called belly-up. It still earns a launch. | I've wasted grand names on some very ordinary leaks.
